# Phase 14f: a simple flat quad, generated by
# tools/generate_primitive_meshes.py (not hand-typed, though a single quad
# is simple enough it could have been -- generated here purely for the same
# one script/one command produces every Create-menu primitive consistency
# sphere.obj already needs a generator for). Half-extent 0.5, centered on its
# own local origin, lying flat on the XZ plane (normal +Y) -- matching
# mesh.hpp's makeGroundPlane() orientation convention.

mtllib plane.mtl

vt 0.000000 0.000000
vt 1.000000 0.000000
vt 1.000000 1.000000
vt 0.000000 1.000000

vn 0.000000 1.000000 0.000000

v -0.500000 0.000000 -0.500000
v 0.500000 0.000000 -0.500000
v 0.500000 0.000000 0.500000
v -0.500000 0.000000 0.500000

o Plane
usemtl Plane
f 4/4/1 3/3/1 2/2/1 1/1/1

